From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt Builder
Date: Sun, 3 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: airoha: fix dev_pm_domain_attach_list return value
 check

dev_pm_domain_attach_list() returns a positive value (the number of
attached PM domains) on success, 0 when no domains are found, and a
negative errno on failure.

The driver incorrectly used `if (ret)` which treats the positive
success return value (1) as an error, causing probe to fail with
"probe with driver airoha-cpufreq failed with error 1".

Fix by checking `if (ret < 0)` to only catch actual errors.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt Builder
---
 drivers/cpufreq/airoha-cpufreq.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/cpufreq/airoha-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/airoha-cpufreq.c
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@
 	/* Attach PM for OPP */
 	ret = dev_pm_domain_attach_list(cpu_dev, &attach_data,
 					&priv->pd_list);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret < 0)
 		goto clear_opp_config;
 
 	cpufreq_dt = platform_device_register_simple("cpufreq-dt", -1, NULL, 0);
